      <div class="prose-summary">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>The tools run in your browser. The files and text that you open in a tool are processed on your device and are never sent to Us.</li>
          <li>There are no accounts, no payments and no cookies.</li>
          <li>We count page visits with Plausible, which does not use cookies or collect Personal Data.</li>
          <li>If You sign up for the newsletter, Mailchimp stores Your email address.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p>This Privacy Policy describes Our policies and procedures on the collection, use and disclosure of Your information when You use the Service and tells You about Your privacy rights and how the law protects You.</p>
      <p>By using the Service, You agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this Privacy Policy.</p>

      <h2>Interpretation and Definitions</h2>

      <h3>Interpretation</h3>
      <p>The words of which the initial letter is capitalized have meanings defined under the following conditions. The following definitions shall have the same meaning regardless of whether they appear in singular or in plural.</p>

      <h3>Definitions</h3>
      <p>For the purposes of this Privacy Policy:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Company</strong> (referred to as either "the Company", "We", "Us" or "Our" in this Policy) refers to Twenty Four Twelve Systems Pte. Ltd., 101 Upper Cross Street, #05-16 People's Park Centre, Singapore.</li>
        <li><strong>Country</strong> refers to: Singapore.</li>
        <li><strong>Device</strong> means any device that can access the Service such as a computer, a cellphone or a digital tablet.</li>
        <li><strong>Personal Data</strong> is any information that relates to an identified or identifiable individual.</li>
        <li><strong>Service</strong> refers to the Website and the tools on it.</li>
        <li><strong>Service Provider</strong> means any natural or legal person who processes data on behalf of the Company.</li>
        <li><strong>Usage Data</strong> refers to data collected automatically when You use the Service.</li>
        <li><strong>Website</strong> refers to [REDACTED], accessible from <a href="https://www.redacted.to">https://www.redacted.to</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Your Content</strong> means the files, images, videos, documents and text that You open, paste or type into a tool.</li>
        <li><strong>You</strong> means the individual accessing or using the Service, or the company, or other legal entity on behalf of which such individual is accessing or using the Service, as applicable.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your Content</h2>
      <p>The tools on the Website process Your Content entirely inside Your web browser, on Your Device. Your Content is not uploaded to, stored on or seen by the Company or any Service Provider. The Website has no server code that receives Your Content.</p>
      <p>To find text, faces and other details, the tools use AI models and libraries that run on Your Device. When You use a tool for the first time, Your browser downloads the model or library it needs and keeps a copy in its cache. These downloads contain only the model or library. They do not contain Your Content.</p>
      <p>Files that You download from a tool are made on Your Device. Where a tool says so, they do not keep the metadata of the original file. You are responsible for checking a result before You share it, because automatic detection can miss information.</p>

      <h2>Collecting and Using Your Personal Data</h2>

      <h3>Types of Data Collected</h3>

      <h4>Personal Data</h4>
      <p>The Service has no accounts and does not ask You for Personal Data, with one exception: if You choose to sign up for the newsletter, You give Your email address to Our email service provider (see "Email Marketing" below).</p>

      <h4>Usage Data</h4>
      <p>We use Plausible Analytics to count visits to the Website. Plausible does not use cookies, does not collect Personal Data and does not track You across websites. It records information such as the pages You visit, the referring website, Your browser, operating system and device type, and Your country. Your IP address is used only to count unique visitors for one day, and is not stored. More information: <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://plausible.io/data-policy</a>.</p>
      <p>Like all websites, the servers that deliver the Website and its files receive technical information with each request, such as Your IP address, browser type and the time of the request. This is described under "Service Providers" below.</p>

      <h3>Cookies and Browser Storage</h3>
      <p>The Website does not use cookies.</p>
      <p>Some tools use Your browser's local storage to remember a choice that You made, for example that You turned on AI detection, so the model can load automatically next time. This information stays on Your Device and is never sent to Us. You can clear it at any time in Your browser settings.</p>

      <h3>Use of Your Personal Data</h3>
      <p>The Company may use Personal Data for the following purposes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>To provide and maintain the Service</strong>, including to monitor the usage of the Service.</li>
        <li><strong>To contact You</strong>: to send the newsletter to You if You signed up for it.</li>
        <li><strong>To manage Your requests</strong>: to answer messages that You send Us.</li>
        <li><strong>For other purposes</strong>: such as data analysis and identifying usage trends, using Usage Data that does not identify You.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell Your Personal Data. We may share Your Personal Data in the following situations:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>With Service Providers</strong>: to deliver the Website, to count visits and to send the newsletter, as described below.</li>
        <li><strong>For business transfers</strong>: in connection with, or during negotiations of, any merger, sale of Company assets, financing, or acquisition of all or a portion of Our business to another company.</li>
        <li><strong>With Your consent</strong>: for any other purpose with Your consent.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Retention of Your Personal Data</h3>
      <p>The Company will retain Your Personal Data only for as long as is necessary for the purposes set out in this Privacy Policy. Your newsletter email address is kept until You unsubscribe. We will retain and use Personal Data to the extent necessary to comply with our legal obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce our legal agreements and policies.</p>

      <h3>Transfer of Your Personal Data</h3>
      <p>Your information, including Personal Data, is processed at the Company's operating offices and in any other places where the parties involved in the processing are located. It means that this information may be transferred to, and maintained on, computers located outside of Your state, province, country or other governmental jurisdiction where the data protection laws may differ from those of Your jurisdiction.</p>
      <p>The Company will take all steps reasonably necessary to ensure that Your data is treated securely and in accordance with this Privacy Policy.</p>

      <h3>Disclosure of Your Personal Data</h3>

      <h4>Business Transactions</h4>
      <p>If the Company is involved in a merger, acquisition or asset sale, Your Personal Data may be transferred. We will provide notice before Your Personal Data is transferred and becomes subject to a different Privacy Policy.</p>

      <h4>Law Enforcement</h4>
      <p>Under certain circumstances, the Company may be required to disclose Your Personal Data if required to do so by law or in response to valid requests by public authorities (e.g. a court or a government agency). Because Your Content never reaches Us, We cannot disclose it.</p>

      <h4>Other Legal Requirements</h4>
      <p>The Company may disclose Your Personal Data in the good faith belief that such action is necessary to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Comply with a legal obligation</li>
        <li>Protect and defend the rights or property of the Company</li>
        <li>Prevent or investigate possible wrongdoing in connection with the Service</li>
        <li>Protect the personal safety of Users of the Service or the public</li>
        <li>Protect against legal liability</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Security of Your Personal Data</h3>
      <p>The security of Your Personal Data is important to Us, but remember that no method of transmission over the Internet, or method of electronic storage is 100% secure. While We strive to use commercially acceptable means to protect Your Personal Data, We cannot guarantee its absolute security.</p>

      <h2>Service Providers</h2>
      <p>The Service Providers We use may have access to limited information about Your visit. They collect, store, use, process and transfer that information in accordance with their own Privacy Policies.</p>

      <h3>Hosting</h3>
      <p><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts and delivers the Website. Their Privacy Policy can be viewed at <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/</a>.</p>

      <h3>Model and Library Downloads</h3>
      <p>The tools download AI models and code libraries from <strong>jsDelivr</strong> (<a href="https://www.jsdelivr.com/terms/privacy-policy-jsdelivr-net" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>) and <strong>Hugging Face</strong> (<a href="https://huggingface.co/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>). These providers receive the technical information that Your browser sends with each download, such as Your IP address. They do not receive Your Content.</p>

      <h3>Analytics</h3>
      <p><strong>Plausible Analytics</strong> counts visits without cookies, as described above. Their data policy can be viewed at <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://plausible.io/data-policy</a>.</p>

      <h3>Email Marketing</h3>
      <p>We may use Your Personal Data to contact You with newsletters about new tools and other information that may be of interest to You, if You signed up for it. You may opt out of receiving any, or all, of these communications from Us by following the unsubscribe link in any email We send or by contacting Us.</p>
      <p><strong>Mailchimp</strong> is an email marketing service provided by The Rocket Science Group LLC. The newsletter sign-up form is on a Mailchimp page. For more information on the privacy practices of Mailchimp, please visit their Privacy Policy: <a href="https://mailchimp.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://mailchimp.com/legal/privacy/</a>.</p>

      <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>Our Service does not address anyone under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from anyone under the age of 13. If You are a parent or guardian and You are aware that Your child has provided Us with Personal Data, please contact Us. If We become aware that We have collected Personal Data from anyone under the age of 13 without verification of parental consent, We take steps to remove that information.</p>

      <h2>Links to Other Websites</h2>
      <p>Our Service may contain links to other websites that are not operated by Us. If You click on a third party link, You will be directed to that third party's site. We strongly advise You to review the Privacy Policy of every site You visit.</p>
      <p>We have no control over and assume no responsibility for the content, privacy policies or practices of any third party sites or services.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>We may update Our Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify You of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page and updating the "Last updated" date at the top of this Privacy Policy.</p>
      <p>You are advised to review this Privacy Policy periodically for any changes. Changes to this Privacy Policy are effective when they are posted on this page.</p>

      <h2>Contact Us</h2>
      <p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, You can contact us by email: <a href="mailto:jon@redacted.to">jon@redacted.to</a></p>
